{title: 088 - I Sing the Mighty Power of God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #088 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 88}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I sing the mighty power of God, [G/B]That [Am]made the mountains [C]rise,
[C]That spread the flowing seas abroad, And built the [G/B]lofty [Am]skies
[Am]I sing [G]the [C]wisdom [G7/B]that ordained The [C]sun to rule [G7]the day;
[G7]The moon shines [C]full [G]at His [C]command And all the [F]stars obey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]I sing the goodness [G/B]of [Am]the [G]Lord,
[C]who filled the earth [Am]with food,
[C]who formed the creatures thru [G/B]the [Am]Word,
[C]and then pronounced them [Am]good.
[Am]Lord, [C]how [G7/B]thy wonders [C/E]are [G7]displayed,
[Am]where'er [G7/B]I turn [C]my eye,
[G7]if I [C]survey the ground [F]I tread,
[G7]or [C]gaze [G]upon [C]the [F]sky!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]There's not a plant or [G/B]flower [Am]below,
[C]but makes thy [G/B]glories known,
[C]and clouds arise, and tempests [Am]blow,
[C]by order from thy [Am]thrown;
[Am]while [C]all [G7/B]that borrows [C]life from [G7]thee
[Am]is [C]ever [G7]in [C]thy care;
[G7]and everywhere [C]that we [F]can be,
[G7]thou, [C]God, [G]art [C]present [F]there.
{end_of_verse}
